<% content_for :head do %>
<style>
 .demo{margin:1.5rem;max-width:760px}
 #presence{margin:.4rem 0;min-height:1.5rem}.chip{color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12px;margin-right:4px}
 .row{display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.5rem 0}
 #progress{font-size:.9rem;color:#374151}
 .row button{border:1px solid #d1d5db;background:#fff;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font:13px system-ui;padding:4px 10px}
 .row button[disabled]{opacity:.55;cursor:default}
 #grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(9,2.6rem);border:2px solid #111;width:max-content;user-select:none}
 .cell{position:relative;height:2.6rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font:20px system-ui;color:#1d4ed8;border:1px solid #d1d5db;background:#fff;cursor:pointer;box-sizing:border-box}
 .cell.br{border-right:2px solid #111}.cell.bb{border-bottom:2px solid #111}
 .cell.given{background:#f3f4f6;color:#111;font-weight:600;cursor:default}
 .cell:focus{outline:2px solid #2563eb;outline-offset:-2px}
 .cell.conflict{background:#fee2e2;color:#b91c1c}
 .cell.here{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 3px var(--c)}
 .cell.here::after{content:attr(data-who);position:absolute;top:0;right:0;font:9px/1 system-ui;padding:2px 3px;background:var(--c);color:#fff;border-radius:0 0 0 4px;white-space:nowrap}
</style>
<% end %>
<div class="demo">
  <header>
    <h1>Co-op sudoku</h1>
    <%= render "nav" %>
    <p>
      Opaque state is a <code>Y.Map</code> keyed by cell. Click a cell and type a
      digit, in two windows. Different cells merge; the same cell is last-writer-wins,
      which is what you want when you are solving together. The puzzle is a second map
      the server wrote once; its cells stay as they are.
    </p>
    <p>
      The checker is a Ruby process that joins as a player over the same websocket
      (<code>SudokuPeer</code>). It reads the grid after each burst of edits and writes
      what it finds into the document: the clashing cells, the count, and a correct
      digit when you ask for a hint. This page only draws what is in the document.
    </p>
    <div id="presence"></div>
    <p id="status" class="status">connecting…</p>
  </header>
  <div class="row">
    <span id="progress">not checked yet</span>
    <button type="button" id="hint">Ask for a hint</button>
    <%= button_to "Invite the checker", document_sudoku_checker_path(@document_id), class: "invite-checker", form: { style: "display:inline" } %>
  </div>
  <div id="grid" role="grid" aria-label="Sudoku" data-document-id="<%= @document_id %>:sudoku"></div>
</div>
<script src="/sudoku.js" defer></script>
